  Every module but RANGEMAP is extracted from krust's KORE (the inputs the script names,
  findings/work/p23; FLOAT's text is krust's KORE of wasm-semantics); FLOAT's 41 symbols are numbered
  as the extraction numbers a module's (after INT-COMMON's, before STRING-COMMON's, in the text's
  order). JSON-SYNTAX's subsorts are those K's json.md declares (`DECLARED_SUBSORTS`: a
  definition's own productions can add more into its sorts, as KEVM's `Int < JSONKey`,
  `Bytes < JSON` and `Map < JSON`).
  RANGEMAP is added by the script's add-module mode from K 7.1.337's kompile of
  prelude/rangemap-probe.k (prelude/add-rangemap.sh): its sentences in K's layout (`[a, b]`, where
  krust writes `[ a, b ]`; both parse to the same KORE). Its sorts and symbols have the numbers
  `APPENDED` gives them, after every other module's, its sorts' `isX` and `project:X` after its
  symbols.
  Builtins.lean reads it.
-/
